Subject: [PATCH] Recognise the GTX IR receiver when TuxTxt takes input

The Linux input name of the receiver is meson-ir. A substring match
for "key" selects the unrelated voice-activity keypad on this board.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [GTX-specific input assignment]

--- a/tuxtxt.c
+++ b/tuxtxt.c
@@ -225,5 +225,5 @@
 		}
 		if (ioctl(rc[rc_num], EVIOCGNAME(128), tmp) < 0)
 			perror("EVIOCGNAME failed");
-		if (!strstr(tmp, "remote control") && !strstr(tmp, "key"))
+		if (strcmp(tmp, "meson-ir") && !strstr(tmp, "remote control"))
 		{
